<form class="totalform help-on-hover help-box" data-method="POST" data-route="/admin/settings/xmlrpc"><div class="form-field toggle-field " data-type="toggle" style="--grid-area: enable;"><label for="field-UID">Enable XML-RPC Publishing</label><div class="form-group"><div class="switch"><input id="field-UID" name="enable" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="help-UID"/><label for="field-UID" aria-hidden="true">Enable XML-RPC Publishing</label></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Master switch. When off, <code>/xmlrpc.php</code> and <code>/xmlrpc/{collection}</code> return 404 — indistinguishable from a site without the feature. Off by default because an exposed <code>xmlrpc.php</code> is a standard security-scanner finding.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: ratePerIp;"><label for="field-UID">Rate Limit (per minute per IP)</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="ratePerIp" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="60" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="60" min="0" max="6000" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Maximum XML-RPC requests per minute from one IP address. The XML parser runs before credentials are checked, so this bounds how much work an anonymous caller can force. Set to <code>0</code> to disable.</p></div><div class="form-inline-fields"><button type="submit" class="button btn cms-save cms-button">Save Settings</button></div></form>